-# Implementation: F-006 boat passenger yaw refresh
-
-Status: implemented; independent re-review pending.
-
-## Finding and source evidence
-
-- Accepted finding snapshot: commit `064fc24e5e3d8b4dab4f12c2000dcb13d37514ca`, `workflows/source-campaign-2026-10-07/1.17.1--1.18.2/findings/F-006-boat-passenger-yaw-refresh.md`, SHA-256 `3994115e3789a8280aa61228b2b092a007e57985cde72492f19731a8f150db95`.
-- Blind source review: commit `4ff925e4e4186adb704d57d9b3471c559945436c`.
-- Pair discovery remains partial; acceptance releases this finding only.
-- 1.17.1 Mojmap source: `LocalPlayer#startRiding` SHA-256 `c9a91cb6cb57806bc8d22e5bfe2d97daaf21d5d2a48f34a6e2c53164c61c5812`; `ClientPacketListener#handleSetEntityPassengersPacket` SHA-256 `a59ba067bb0b9cdf026159a87534fd456ed766ec287cfd23e24356f84f078a5a`.
-- 1.18.2 Mojmap source: `LocalPlayer#startRiding` SHA-256 `99c2d18bcd23243afb8f95c5bafb21fb0be7ea04aacbb14fcf7be7ced2c9c095`; `ClientPacketListener#handleSetEntityPassengersPacket` SHA-256 `e718016022c2ae86a2c354af2d34fe4de7d6e36dc8792d2e2c1f08abb6b77b7b`.
-- Current 26.2 unobfuscated source: `ClientPacketListener.java` SHA-256 `9cb0cc8afebae9f4e42f428a52719c645817d03893dc371e6711c7bd16eac1b6`; `LocalPlayer.java` SHA-256 `8d089aa09217e3607b38590f7c1623385562800943ac6dfd3d17804e041da6d6`.
-
-## Implementation
-
-- The reusable client bridge is `ClientPacketListenerMixin`; its existing pre-rebuild check stays `vehicle.hasIndirectPassenger(player)`, matching the modern packet handler and retaining nested-to-direct transitions.
-- During `handleSetEntityPassengersPacket`, a wrapper records only a successful `Entity#startRiding(Entity, boolean, boolean)` call where the passenger is the local player and the vehicle is the captured boat. The TAIL dispatch now requires both that event and the pre-packet indirect-membership guard. Nested riders that remain nested do not trigger the old yaw reset.
-- The TAIL hook remains after the packet's passenger-list rebuild. The handler's main-thread check runs before passenger lookup/ejection; unknown-vehicle handling reaches TAIL without a captured refresh. Initial direct mounts have no pre-packet membership and continue through vanilla's native mount yaw write. The correction writes only current movement-facing `yRot`; interpolation and head-yaw fields remain excluded.
-- The `V1_17_1` change stays exact-profile guarded. `ChangeResolver` selects the closest registered change whose `emulates` ordinal is at least the selected profile, and returns no changes for `CURRENT`; therefore the correction is limited to the 1.17.1 profile and native movement is unchanged.
-
-## Verification and handoff
-
-- Static review: exact 26.2 packet-handler descriptor and operation order checked against the shared unobfuscated source; `git diff --check` passed.
-- Build, tests, clients, TAS, servers, and Docker were not run, per assignment.
-- Runtime parity remains unvalidated. Independent re-review is pending.
-- Task branch: `feat/movement-passenger-yaw-2026-10-08`, based on handoff commit `48003fe0cf923529cf65358dd96126a918e436eb`.
